.nh
.TH "GHPM" "1" "Nov 2026" "ghpm" "ghpm manual"

.SH NAME
ghpm-completion-bash - Generate the autocompletion script for bash


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBghpm completion bash\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate the autocompletion script for the bash shell.

.PP
This script depends on the 'bash-completion' package.
If it is not installed already, you can install it via your OS's package manager.

.PP
To load completions in your current shell session:

.EX
source <(ghpm completion bash)
.EE

.PP
To load completions for every new session, execute once:

.SS Linux:
.EX
ghpm completion bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/ghpm
.EE

.SS macOS:
.EX
ghpm completion bash > $(brew --prefix)/etc/bash_completion.d/ghpm
.EE

.PP
You will need to start a new shell for this setup to take effect.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for bash

.PP
\fB--no-descriptions\fP[=false]
	disable completion descriptions


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default ~/.config/ghpm/config.yaml)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine readable output (where supported)

.PP
\fB--no-cache\fP[=false]
	bypass the release metadata cache

.PP
\fB--proxy\fP=""
	HTTP(S) proxy URL, overrides config


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBghpm-completion(1)\fP
